In types.ts:
```ts
export type MailEvent = 'case-invited'|'review-assigned'|'op-raised'|'op-answered'|'op-returned'|'op-edited'|'op-closed'|'release-requested'|'release-withdrawn'|'case-completed'|'release-receipt'|'case-cancelled'|'case-reactivated';
export interface Mail {
  id: string; at: string; event: MailEvent;
  audience: Side;
  to: string[]; cc?: string[];
  subject: string; body: string;
  caseId: string; openPointId?: string; documentId?: string;
  link: string;
  channel: 'open-point-webhook'|'task-notification'|'final-document';
  readBy: string[];
}
```
- `audience` is never mixed in one mail.
- `to` and `cc` hold user ids, resolved to e-mails for display.
- `link` is the in-app route the button opens.
- `channel` names the final-app mechanism: R-1 generic webhook, native or portal task e-mail, or the AS-12 release script.
- `id` is `M-0001`, from mail.length + 1, so it is deterministic.

`AppState.mail: Mail[]` is required. LiveSupplierStore.tsx:266 adds `mail: []`, a one-line portal change.

Add `CiqCase.finalDocument?: FinalDocument` (optional, so map.ts compiles).

```ts
interface FinalDocument {
  id: string;
  caseId: string;
  fileName: string;
  generatedAt: string;
  trigger: 'final-release';
  generatedBy: 'system';
  fingerprint: string;
  header: { caseId; materialName; inci; materialNo; supplierName; supplierDuns; manufacturer; site; ownerName; createdAt; templateVersion; ruleSetVersion; markets: Market[] };
  metadata: { id: ConfigQuestionId; code; label; value: string }[];
  sections: { sectionId; code; title; applicability: 'mandatory'|'optional'; addedLater: boolean; reason: string; fields: { fieldId; label; value: string; justification?: string; by?: string; at?: string }[] }[];
  components: ComponentRow[];
  waivers: { key; label; text }[];
  evidence: { name; kind; section: string; field?: string; uploadedBy: string; uploadedAt: string; sizeKb: number }[];
  openPoints: { id; kind; raisedBy: string; raisedAt; ref: string; question: string; outcome: string; closedBy?; closedAt?; rounds: number; thread: { at; by: string; side: Side; action: string; text: string; document?: string; internal: boolean }[]; changes: { at; by; text }[] }[];
  confirmations: Confirmation[];
}
```

Field notes:
- `id`: `${caseId}-FINAL`.
- `fileName`: `${caseId}_CIQ_final.pdf`, with no review version.
- `generatedAt`: the release time.
- `fingerprint`: FNV-1a 32-bit hex over the canonical JSON of the document without the fingerprint, shown as 'Document fingerprint'.
- `metadata`: SF-01 to SF-12 as released.
- `sections`: only sections that are not N.A.
- `waivers`: K5.1 and other justifications.
- `evidence`: a list only, no attachments (R-2).
- `openPoints`: every point, every message as text. For a document the thread holds 'name (uploaded date)' only; `internal` is true for the not-accepted note. `changes` holds the AS-08 edit history.
- `confirmations`: completeness, every dept-completion (RMM's included) and final-release, in time order.

Build it with the pure `buildFinalDocument(state, c, at)` in src/domain/finalDocument.ts. complete() calls it after the final-release confirmation. Then:
- audit 'Generated final document' with fileName and fingerprint;
- mail case-completed to the RMM owner, carrying documentId;
- audit 'Filed final document at the case; B-Flow filing manual in the MVP'.

Also export `verifyFinalDocument(doc): boolean`, which recomputes the fingerprint. The document is internal: suppliers never see it. Supplier release receipt: 'Beiersdorf has filed the final document.'

**In:**
- answers of mandatory and optional active sections at release time;
- K2.1 rows;
- justifications instead of values ('Not provided: <justification>');
- the evidence list with uploader and upload date;
- every open point, withdrawn and not-accepted included, with all rounds, edits, returns and cannot-provide in order, with who, when and the reference label (R-2);
- the three confirmation kinds;
- the CIQ ID;
- the template and rule-set versions.

**Out:**
- answers kept in sections that closed before completeness (AS-03 keeps them in c.answers but they are not released);
- attachments themselves;
- internal notes (REQ-PROC-020);
- RMES criteria, findings and decisions (not in REQ-PROC-046; open question to Beiersdorf, E-P-71).

It is generated exactly once. A second finalRelease is refused with 'This CIQ is already released' (today actions.ts:568 gives the misleading 'requested only after…' message).

Selector `managerOf(op) = op.createdBy === 'system' ? op.responsibleId : op.createdBy`, and `canManagePoint(state, userId, op)`.

**editOpenPoint(s, by, caseId, opId, patch: { question?, justification?, dueDate?, ref?, kind? }, at)**

Guards:
- guardOpen;
- by === managerOf(op), otherwise toast 'Only <name>, who raised OP-…, can change it';
- op not closed;
- at least one real change;
- the question is not blank;
- dueDate ≥ today.

Effects:
- update the fields; push history 'edited'; push the thread message 'edited';
- if the question or reference changed while the point is in-progress (already answered): status → open, rounds + 1, the raising track → waiting-supplier (the supplier must answer the changed question);
- a change to the due date or justification alone keeps the status;
- audit 'Changed open point';
- mail op-edited.

**closeOpenPoint(s, by, caseId, opId, outcome, reason, at)**

The outcome is 'accepted', 'not-accepted' or 'withdrawn'. Guards: guardOpen and raiser only. 'accepted' and 'not-accepted' require status in-progress. 'withdrawn' is allowed from open or in-progress. not-accepted and withdrawn require a reason.

Effects:
- status closed with outcome, closedBy and closedAt;
- history 'closed';
- a thread message: accepted (visible), note (internal) or withdrawn (visible);
- track status recomputed as in actions.ts:454;
- not-accepted on SAF or REG adds the closed finding as today (actions.ts:457-459);
- audit;
- mail op-closed.

reviewResponse keeps 'return' with the same raiser guard, plus a guard that the status is in-progress. Its accept and not-accepted paths delegate to closeOpenPoint. The supplier view updates through the shared store, which stands in for the final app's portal update by integration.

Unit test: kpis(buildDemoStart()) returns all zeros, and pipeline and deptWorkload return arrays with zero counts.

Harness P00 asserts on every persona's landing page and every nav page:
- the body text contains none of 'NaN', 'Infinity', 'undefined' or 'Invalid Date';
- each list shows its empty-state testid: empty-dashboard, empty-cases, empty-reviews, empty-informed, empty-reports, empty-audit, empty-portal, empty-tasks, empty-mail;
- there are no page errors or console errors.

New files:
- **seed.demo.test.ts:**
  - 0 cases and 0 mails;
  - 1 supplier with 2 active mayConfirm contacts;
  - one user per internal persona;
  - personasOf has 11 + 2 entries, and every persona resolves;
  - every user id referenced exists;
  - deterministic (JSON equal on two builds);
  - SCHEMA === 7 and seedStub SCHEMA === SCHEMA.
- **persist.test.ts:** invalid JSON, schema 6, an unknown persona, a deactivated-contact persona and missing arrays each give the empty start; valid state round-trips without toasts.
- **suppliers.test.ts:** the S-02 rules (8-digit DUNS, letters, '012 345-678' kept with its leading zero, duplicate DUNS against an inactive supplier, duplicate e-mail against an internal or a foreign contact, name warning plus ack), the S-03 deactivation rules, and permission refusal for REG.
- **personas.test.ts:** a new contact appears as sup:<id>, an inactive one disappears, legacy aliases resolve.
- **mail.test.ts:**
  - every M-02 row, recipients exact;
  - exactly one release-requested across N completions;
  - a withdrawn and re-sent request gives 2 mails in total;
  - supplier bodies are free of planted sentinels (internal note, finding text, not-accepted reason, cancellation reason) and of the department labels in DEPT_LABEL;
  - 'Sent e-mail' audit per mail;
  - read state per user.
- **openPoints.test.ts:** the O-02 and O-03 rules, including a non-raiser in the same department, the RMM owner, another department, a closed point, a past due date, a no-op edit, an edit of an answered point reopening it, withdraw unblocking completeReview, a system additional part managed by its responsible person, and supplierRespond on a closed point refused.
- **finalDocument.test.ts:** run from buildDemoStart through the domain only (testkit). Assert the F-01 and F-02 content: the CIQ ID; the field count equals the released answered fields; the closed-section answer is excluded; all thread messages appear in order; the three confirmation kinds; verifyFinalDocument is true; the mail to the owner carries documentId; the F-03 freeze guards each refuse and log while the document stays deep-equal.
- **permissions.test.ts:** the whole matrix.

Shared helper src/domain/testkit.ts, imported only by tests and the fixtures script:
- `fillAllRequired(state, caseId, by)`, a generic value per FieldDef type plus components, reusing the scenario valueFor;
- `toReview(state, …)`;
- `completeAllTracks(state, caseId)`, covering RMES results and decisions.
